# Magical Mystery Tour, instrumental bridge: ten bars (figure 122.4).
# Pollack types "f" in bar 3 with "ii7" under it; read as f# (ii7 of E), as in the second system.
# The G# in bar 8 is the syncopated bass note the essay describes, falling on the "and" of beat 3
# by Pollack's beat count "1 2 3& 4" (kept as a words row). To show it as a bass note, the system
# gets a bass row; its B and F# are added (the chord roots), not typed by Pollack.
key E

system
chords   | B{E: V} | - | f#{ii7} | - |

system
words             | r | r | r | 1 2 3*0.5 &*0.5 4 |
bass              | B2 | - | F#2 | -*2.5 G#2*1.5 |
chords            | B{V} | - | f#{ii7} | - |

system
chords   | A{IV} | B{V} |
